    "title": "Bridge demolition begins on State Route 75 near Town Creek - NewsBreak",
    "text": "DEKALB COUNTY, Ala. (WHNT) — The Alabama Department of Transportation says contractors began demolishing the 83-year-old bridge over Town Creek at Lakeview on Wednesday. Traffic recently shifted from the old bridge on State Route 75 onto a newly built bridge . ALDOT said that the new bridge was the product of a $13.7 million construction project. The agency said the new bridge is wider, longer and taller, and features defined shoulders while also correcting steep vertical curves that were on the old bridge going either direction. With the new bridge up and running, ALDOT said the demolition of the old bridge, which was originally built in 1942, is underway. The agency said the plan is to remove the bridge piece by piece to limit the disturbance to the creek below it. ALDOT said it anticipates the demolition of the old bridge and removal of the old bits of roadway on either side to be completed this fall, bringing an end to the bridge replacement project, which started in 2023. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WHNT.com.",
